# Code owners for toxindb.
#
# Honest caveat: this project has exactly one maintainer, so every rule below
# resolves to the same person and this file currently routes nothing. Its
# purpose is to *document* which paths are safety-critical, so that adding a
# second maintainer later is a matter of naming them here rather than
# rediscovering the blast radius. Treat it as intent, not as enforcement: the
# rules only gate anything once `main` has branch protection, which it does not
# yet have.
#
# The paths that matter most are the detection and trace-schema files. A change
# that makes a heuristic stop firing, or that changes how a trace is parsed,
# breaks the project's premise and would not be caught by any other signal.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                               @5h4d0wn1k

# The heuristics themselves. Each TX-NNN gates whether a poisoning pattern is
# detected at all, so changes here need the owner and a test that proves the
# heuristic still fires on a poison trace and stays quiet on a clean one.
/toxindb/heuristics.py         @5h4d0wn1k
/toxindb/engine.py             @5h4d0wn1k
/toxindb/canary.py             @5h4d0wn1k
/toxindb/provenance.py         @5h4d0wn1k

# Trace parsing and the input schema. A silent schema change here would make
# every heuristic wrong at once without any of them failing their own test.
/toxindb/trace.py              @5h4d0wn1k
/toxindb/trace_gen.py          @5h4d0wn1k

# Detection output. Report/alert formats are consumed by other tooling.
/toxindb/report.py             @5h4d0wn1k
/toxindb/cli.py                @5h4d0wn1k

